.TH "speedtest-cli" 1 "2026-04-20" "speedtest-cli"
.SH NAME
speedtest\-cli \- Command line interface for testing internet bandwidth using speedtest.net
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B speedtest\-cli
[OPTION...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Speedtest.net is a web service for testing your broadband connection by downloading a file
from a nearby speedtest.net server on the web. This tool allows you to access the service
from the command line.

Speedtest mini is a version of the Speedtest.net server that you can host locally.

.SH OPTIONS
Usage: speedtest\-cli [OPTION...]

.B Help Options

\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
.RS
Displays usage for the tool.
.RE

.B Options

\fB\-\-no\-download\fR
.RS
Do not perform download test
.RE

\fB\-\-no\-upload\fR
.RS
Do not perform upload test
.RE

\fB\-\-single\fR
.RS
Only use a single connection instead of multiple. This simulates a typical file transfer.
.RE

\fB\-\-bytes\fR
.RS
Display values in bytes instead of bits. Does not affect the image generated by \-\-share, nor output from \-\-json or \-\-csv
.RE

\fB\-\-share\fR
.RS
Generate and provide a URL to the speedtest.net share results image, not displayed with \-\-csv
.RE

\fB\-\-simple\fR
.RS
Suppress verbose output, only show basic information
.RE

\fB\-\-csv\fR
.RS
Suppress verbose output, only show basic information in CSV format. Speeds listed in bit/s and not affected by \-\-bytes
.RE

\fB\-\-csv\-delimiter CSV_DELIMITER\fR
.RS
Single character delimiter to use in CSV output. Default ","
.RE

\fB\-\-csv\-header\fR
.RS
Print CSV headers
.RE

\fB\-\-json\fR
.RS
Suppress verbose output, only show basic information in JSON format. Speeds listed in bit/s and not affected by \-\-bytes
.RE

\fB\-\-list\fR
.RS
Display a list of speedtest.net servers sorted by distance
.RE

\fB\-\-server SERVER\fR
.RS
Specify a server ID to test against. Can be supplied multiple times
.RE

\fB\-\-exclude EXCLUDE\fR
.RS
Exclude a server from selection. Can be supplied multiple times
.RE

\fB\-\-mini MINI\fR
.RS
URL of the Speedtest Mini server
.RE

\fB\-\-source SOURCE\fR
.RS
Source IP address to bind to
.RE

\fB\-\-timeout TIMEOUT\fR
.RS
HTTP timeout in seconds. Default 10
.RE

\fB\-\-secure\fR
.RS
Use HTTPS when communicating with speedtest.net operated servers. This is the default and is kept for backward compatibility.
.RE

\fB\-\-no\-secure\fR
.RS
Use HTTP instead of HTTPS. Not recommended \- speedtest.net may reject plain HTTP requests and results can be tampered with in transit.
.RE

\fB\-\-no\-pre\-allocate\fR
.RS
Do not pre allocate upload data. Pre allocation is enabled by default to improve upload performance. To support systems with insufficient memory, use this option to avoid a MemoryError
.RE

\fB\-\-version\fR
.RS
Show the version number and exit
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES

\fBAutomatically find closest server and start testing\fR
.RS
speedtest\-cli
.RE

\fBConcise one-line summary\fR
.RS
speedtest\-cli \-\-simple
.RE

\fBMachine-readable JSON output for logging\fR
.RS
speedtest\-cli \-\-json
.RE

\fBCSV with a custom delimiter\fR
.RS
speedtest\-cli \-\-csv \-\-csv\-delimiter ';'
.RE

\fBSpecify testing against server 1491\fR
.RS
speedtest\-cli \-\-server 1491
.RE

\fBList servers sorted by distance, then test against one\fR
.RS
speedtest\-cli \-\-list
.br
speedtest\-cli \-\-server 1491
.RE

\fBTesting against Speedtest Mini\fR
.RS
speedtest\-cli \-\-mini http://speedtest.local/mini
.RE

\fBBind to a specific source IP address\fR
.RS
speedtest\-cli \-\-source 192.168.1.100
.RE

.SH NOTES
All traffic to speedtest.net-operated hosts uses HTTPS by default as of
speedtest\-cli 2.1.4. The \fB\-\-secure\fR flag is retained as a no-op
for backward compatibility; \fB\-\-no\-secure\fR opts out but is not
recommended because speedtest.net may reject plain-HTTP requests and
results cannot be trusted against an on-path attacker.

If the \fBdefusedxml\fR package is installed, it is used for parsing
the speedtest.net XML responses as a defence-in-depth measure. This is
optional; the standard library parser is used when \fBdefusedxml\fR
is not available.

.SH SEE ALSO
speedtest.net(1) web interface at https://www.speedtest.net/

